# Internal working/planning docs — NEVER git-controlled. Put any private draft,
# strategy note, dogfood plan, or results write-up under internal/ and it is
# ignored automatically (no per-file maintenance). Polished PUBLIC docs go in
# docs/ or ROADMAP.md, not here. (The old root-level sidecar-*.md / PLAN.md were
# moved into internal/; they remain in git history — this only stops future
# tracking.)
/internal/

# Stryker mutation-testing sandboxes (transient; can be 50MB+ and are
# recreated on every run). Stryker ignores them internally, git did not —
# a `git add -A` after a run swept 1117 sandbox files into a commit.
.stryker-tmp/
